# Docker & Makefile

## Daily workflow

```bash
make dev          # Start full dev stack with hot reload
make dev-rebuild  # After package.json or Dockerfile changes
make dev-logs     # Follow app logs
make dev-shell    # Shell in app container (requires dev stack running)
make dev-migrate  # Run Drizzle migrations in container
```

## Host + DB only

```bash
make db-up        # PostgreSQL only
pnpm dev          # Nuxt on host
pnpm db:migrate   # Migrations on host
```

## Gotchas

- Dev image is **Debian-based** (not Alpine) — required for native modules
- Container startup runs `nuxt prepare` — do not remove
- The dev entrypoint drops to the host uid that owns the repo (the image `node` user when that uid exists) so `.nuxt` stays writable by host `pnpm`
- After adding npm packages in Docker: `make dev-rebuild` (refreshes the anonymous `node_modules` volume)
- Production binds `127.0.0.1:3000` for reverse proxy use
- `@nuxt/content` SQLite cache lives in the `nuxt_content_cache` Docker volume (not on the host `.data/`). If you see `no such table: _content_*`, run `make dev-content-reset` and wait for the log line `Processed … collections` before opening blog pages
- Host-only dev (`pnpm dev`): delete `.data/content` and restart if content collections were added or queries fail with missing `_content_*` tables

## Staging / production

```bash
make staging-migrate && make staging-up
make prod-migrate && make prod-up
```

Production HTTPS and multi-site VPS: [deploy/README.md](../deploy/README.md).

CrowdSec is optional. `make dev` and `make prod-up` do not start it.

```bash
make crowdsec-up        # Engine + local Caddy bouncer (127.0.0.1:8088)
make crowdsec-down
make crowdsec-prod-up   # Engine only, on the VPS (host Caddy is the bouncer)
```

See `Makefile` for full target list (`make help`).
